#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100662 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "0713e68d-2b3e-5010-954f-7891d96bdbbb" :question/math-academy-id "e-3640" :question/problem "The values of functions $h(x)$ and $z(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=-1$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $h(x)$ | $z(x)$ | $h'(x)$ | $z'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $-4$ | $2$ | $6$ | $3$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\dfrac{h(x)}{z(x)}\\right)$ at $x=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\dfrac{h(x)}{z(x)}\\right) = \\dfrac{h'(x)z(x)-h(x)z'(x)}{(z(x))^2}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{h(x)}{z(x)})|}_{x=-1} & =\\frac{{h}^{′}(-1)z(-1)-h(-1){z}^{′}(-1)}{(z(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 2-(-4)\\cdot 3}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{4} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100663 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "787e9681-8009-5ba8-acda-6d8830397d18" :question/math-academy-id "e-3641" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ we have\n\n$$\nf(1)=2, \\quad f'(1)=2, \\quad g(1)=-1, \\quad g'(1)=3.\n$$\n\nIf  $h(x) = \\left( f(x)-1 \\right)\\left(2g(x)+1\\right),$  compute  $h'(1).$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule states that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big(uv\\Big) = u \\dfrac{\\textrm d v}{\\textrm d x} +v \\dfrac{\\textrm du}{\\textrm d x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=f(x)-1$ and $v=2g(x)+1.$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = f'(x) \\qquad  \\text{and}\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d v}{\\textrm d x} = 2g'(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(x) & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(f(x)-1)\\cdot 2{g}^{′}(x)+(2g(x)+1)\\cdot {f}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =2{g}^{′}(x)(f(x)-1)+{f}^{′}(x)(2g(x)+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(1) & =2{g}^{′}(1)(f(1)-1)+{f}^{′}(1)(2g(1)+1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3\\cdot (2-1)+2\\cdot (2\\cdot (-1)+1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100749 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "a87386d5-4a1b-539c-aeb9-dd60181baa4f" :question/math-academy-id "e-6154" :question/problem "The values of functions $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=-3$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $p(x)$ | $q(x)$ | $p'(x)$ | $q'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $1$ | $8$ | $0$ | $-2$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big( p(x) + 5q(x) \\big)$ at $x=-3.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left( p(x) + 5q(x) \\right) = p'(x) + 5q'(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-3$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(p(x)+5q(x))|}_{x=-3} & ={p}^{′}(-3)+5{q}^{′}(-3) \\\\  & =0+5\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100750 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100920 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Product Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "d1d0a3ec-2a84-580a-968e-53b773510853" :question/math-academy-id "e-6155" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $f'(x)$ | $g'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(f(x)g(x)\\big)$ at $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(f(x)g(x)\\big) = f(x)g'(x)+f'(x)g(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=0} & =f(0){g}^{′}(0)+{f}^{′}(0)g(0) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445186 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc13996b-ed1b-5e8e-a207-d62c584e1725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc13996b-ed1b-5e8e-a207-d62c584e1725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445164} :answer-field/id #uuid "72717550-a6aa-5a9b-8df2-1401d5e8c09c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "820989f9-6d7d-594e-a9c9-c00397b747b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-311283" :question/problem "The values of functions $h(x)$ and $z(x)$ and their derivatives at $t=3$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $h(t)$ | $z(t)$ | ${h}^{′}(t)$ | ${z}^{′}(t)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $-2$ | $6$ | $5$ | $-1$ |\n\nIf $f(t)=\\frac{2+h(t)}{z(t)},$ compute  ${f}^{′}(3).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}^{′}(3)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2+h(t)$ and $v=z(t).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}={h}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}={z}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(t)=\\frac{{h}^{′}(t)z(t)-(2+h(t)){z}^{′}(t)}{{z}^{2}(t)}.\n$$\n\nAt $t=3,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & =\\frac{{h}^{′}(3)z(3)-(2+h(3)){z}^{′}(3)}{{z}^{2}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 6-(2+(-2))(-1)}{{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30-(0)(-1)}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315104 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "290f52b2-20e6-5905-988c-748802b627d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "290f52b2-20e6-5905-988c-748802b627d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312286} :answer-field/id #uuid "c222c8e2-34bd-53c8-8877-54fd0121599e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314556}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9a67f2b8-f03c-57a0-a261-901981830dca" :question/math-academy-id "q-341468" :question/problem "The values of functions $h(t)$ and $z(t)$ and their derivatives at $t=4$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $h(t)$ | $z(t)$ | ${h}^{′}(t)$ | ${z}^{′}(t)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $3$ | $1$ |\n\nIf $f(t)=\\frac{2h(t)-5}{1-z(t)},$ compute ${f}^{′}(4).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}^{′}(4)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2h(t)-5$ and $v=1-z(t).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2{h}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-{z}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2{h}^{′}(t)(1-z(t))-(2h(t)-5)(-{z}^{′}(t))}{(1-z(t))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt $t=4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{2{h}^{′}(4)(1-z(4))-(2h(4)-5)(-{z}^{′}(4))}{(1-z(4))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(3)(1-(-2))-(2(1)-5)(-1)}{(1-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(3)(3)-(-3)(-1)}{(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18-3}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341895 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "158ef797-3c95-5bcd-9718-13a56de44516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339318} {:answer/id #uuid "367510c1-9a7d-5efc-9a23-2d2dab4e5e4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339615} {:answer/id #uuid "4bce8f0b-d42b-5d9d-86f7-87536d507436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339810} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9b66b0-f49d-525c-93bf-5c48acfa8b76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340523} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e6fda6-a5b1-52d7-9e11-0a56fd7ca0a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a9b66b0-f49d-525c-93bf-5c48acfa8b76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340523} :answer-field/id #uuid "02a49899-89cd-5419-a9ac-3c21bb420e9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8bd63bec-2f2e-5dc7-9fc2-4882af93d878" :question/math-academy-id "q-72996" :question/problem "For the functions $e(x)$ and $n(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\ne(-5)=5,\\,{e}^{′}(-5)=-6,\\,n(-5)=-7,\\,{n}^{′}(-5)=9\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3e(x)+n(x))$ at $x=-5.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3e(x)+n(x))=3{e}^{′}(x)+{n}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-5$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3e(x)+n(x))|}_{x=-5} & =3{e}^{′}(-5)+{n}^{′}(-5) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-6)+9 \\\\  & =-18+9 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
